          <p class="text-slate-400 text-xs italic">
            Citing public reports only, not product endorsements.
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed list-disc list-inside">
            <li><strong>Suno v6 (Sep 9)</strong>: Natural language targeted edits for a single guitar line or lyric phrase without full regeneration; stitching stems together; multimodal inputs.</li>
            <li><strong>Suno Studio 2.0</strong>: Multi-track stem separation (Auto Split, Split from Mix, Advanced Split). Only separated layers can be manipulated individually.</li>
            <li><strong>Udio</strong>: Audio, video, and stems download restrictions ongoing since late 2025. Generation does not equal layer-level control.</li>
            <li><strong>Kid Rock Faith Album (Oct 17)</strong>: Billboard report on Kid Rock's album *Halfway 2 Jesus* utilizing Suno for choir arrangements and select orchestral layers. (News report, not production blueprint.)</li>
